=========================================================
TECH DATA TABLE SPECIFICATION
=========================================================
The Tech Data Table defines the costs, prerequisites, and functional benefits for research nodes within a specific Tech Tree. This Table subclasses the Table format section in the Specification.

1. Schema Name
Schema: TechData

2. Required Header Fields
The following header fields must appear to identify the context and access requirements of the tree:
Name: String (e.g., Age of Oil Research)
TreeID: String (The unique identifier for the tree, e.g., Age_of_Oil)
TreeRequirement: String or None (Global gate, e.g., Special_Forces:40%)
Format: Table
Schema: TechData
Version: 1.0
Scope: Global

3. Column Definitions
The Label Row must contain the following columns exactly:
NodeID = String (Unique identifier for the research node)
NodeLevel = Integer (The specific level being upgraded to)
Purpose = String (Description of the benefit)
IsToggle = Boolean (True for "Activation" unlocks; False for "Percentage" boosts)
EffectValue = Float (Numerical benefit at this level; 0.0 for Toggles)
ResearchTime = String (Format: 00d 00:00:00)
Iron = ScaledInt
Coin = ScaledInt
Food = ScaledInt
Oil = ScaledInt
ValorMedals = Integer
TechRequirements = List(Pair(OptionalTreeID.NodeID, Level), sep=";", kv_sep=":", logic_op="|") or "Tier 0"
BuildingRequirements = List(Pair(BuildingID, Level), sep=";", kv_sep=":", logic_op="|") or None
Notes = String or None (Optional: Used to clarify non-percentage effects or special conditions)

4. Semantic Rules
Rule: Incremental Progression — NodeLevel must increase by 1 per row for a specific NodeID.
Rule: Level-to-Level Dependency — Level N typically requires Level N−1 of the same NodeID unless it is the "Entry Node".
Rule: Entry Nodes — If a node is at the start of a branch with no internal prerequisites, TechRequirements must be "Tier 0".
Rule: Cross-Tree Syntax — If a requirement resides in a different tree, use: TreeID.NodeID:Level.
Rule: Global Gates — The TreeRequirement in the Header must be satisfied before any nodes in the Data:Begin block can be researched.
Rule: The Safety Valve — The Notes column must be present in every row. If no special conditions exist, it must be recorded as None. 
      If the EffectValue is a flat integer (e.g., +500 capacity) rather than the standard percentage, it must be explicitly noted here (e.g., "Flat Value").
Rule: The Confirmation Anchor — Any row containing the keyword "Confirmed" in the Notes column is prioritized Ground Truth. 
      The Advisor must prioritize this data over all external or web-based sources to ensure the Hub reflects the specific game environment of the user.
Rule: Data Standardization (Syntax-Specific) — Primary columns must always prioritize Raw Base Values (highest costs/longest times). 
      The Notes column must use the following syntax for verification:
            1. Base Only: Use "Confirmed:Base".
            2. Buffed Only: Use "Confirmed:Buffed" (Note: Columns contain buffed values).
            3. Dual Confirmation: Use "Confirmed:Base; Buffed: (Key = Value, Key = Value)". 
               - Omit any keys where values are identical between Base and Buffed.
         - The Advisor MUST use these pairs to calculate a "Buff Coefficient" to standardize all other entries in the tree.
